{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":12368,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This family includes the TusA sulfurtransferases [[cite:PUB00043028]].","domain_architectures":48,"interpro_id":"IPR001455","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":18447,"name":"Sulfurtransferase TusA","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF01206","proteins":18434,"proteomes":11553,"short_name":"TusA","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF01206","structures":9,"taxa":16830,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","history":[{"action":"CREATE","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Inspected the 2024 primary study, Figure 1 and Figure 5 images, methods and reference identity. Added observed IscS sulfide-production stimulation and a separately scoped concentration-dependent Fe-S assembly optical phenotype. Retained clone, assay and sulfur-diversion uncertainties. Status remains IN_PROGRESS; no publication or complete-family review.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065330Z-codex-51fd09.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065330Z-codex-51fd09.yaml","outcome":"changed","source_path":"history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065330Z-codex-51fd09.yaml","summary":"Curate two scoped E. coli TusA causal assay graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:53:30Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/30a0601c713fdbf1080ab8c2cc0f5ea1ad264f59/history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065330Z-codex-51fd09.yaml"},{"action":"REVIEW","agent":"Codex","curator":"Codex","description":"Reviewed the current two-graph projection, exact reference mapping and primary figures. The report preserves clone/protocol gaps and unreviewed sulfur-relay contexts, and distinguishes an observed optical outcome from a proposed molecular mechanism. Same-agent assessment, not independent approval; IN_PROGRESS retained.","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065734Z-codex-7bfcbc.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"local_source":"source/history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065734Z-codex-7bfcbc.yaml","outcome":"needs_followup","source_path":"history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065734Z-codex-7bfcbc.yaml","summary":"Retain partial scientific self-review of TusA assay graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:57:34Z","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech/blob/30a0601c713fdbf1080ab8c2cc0f5ea1ad264f59/history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065734Z-codex-7bfcbc.yaml"}],"local_source":"source/data/families/PF01206.yaml","record":{"causal_graphs":[{"context":"Figure 1 uses gel-filtered precomplexes formed at a 1:3 IscS-to-partner ratio for 20 min at 30 C in 50 mM Tris-HCl, 200 mM NaCl, pH 8. Activity is measured over 10 min at 30 C with 1 mM DTT and 1 mM L-cysteine by methylene-blue sulfide quantification against Na2S standards. IscS alone and TusA alone are controls. The paper reports BL21(DE3) expression and untagged TusA/IscS for interaction studies; exact Figure 1 protein doses and complete clone sequences remain unverified.","edges":[{"directness":"DIRECT","edge_id":"tusa-increases-iscs-assay-activity","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01206/olivieri-2024-tusa.txt","cache_sha256":"b124297078a284b15112757262281fe7e0edd4cdbc2a60fdd2f07dd1dc14e4ba","explanation":"Figure 1 image, caption, Results and desulfurase Methods support the direction and purified assay scope. TusA-only and IscS-only controls are retained; the optical assay does not trace sulfur to a cellular product.","reference":"PMID:38980029","snippet":"increase in the IscS activity by a factor of about 3","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11302665/"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01206/TusA-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"4e512da52d9b77d458bcf81b447c01eee49eb768089e8010c7d2a75c68abcc32","explanation":"Resolves the reference protein to this family; the mapping is not separate proof of the activity or a sequence-verified experimental clone.","reference":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0A890/entry/pfam/PF01206/","snippet":"Pfam:PF01206; domain interval: 10-79, inclusive","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/protein/uniprot/P0A890/entry/pfam/PF01206/"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"The purified IscS-TusA preparation produces sulfide at about three times the activity of IscS alone under the stated conditions. This is a directly tested protein-dependent biochemical effect, without assigning an elementary catalytic or cellular regulatory mechanism.","object":"iscs-sulfide-production","predicate":"increases","subject":"tusa-present-with-iscs","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"E. coli K12 reference UniProtKB:P0A890 (tusA/sirA/yhhP, b3470/JW3435), sequence version 1, 81 aa, maps to PF01206 at 10-79 inclusive. InterPro and UniProt sequences agree. The cited 2013 protocol lists pJD34, tusA in pET11b; the 2024 cloning template strain is not independently verified. BL21 is the expression host, not an inferred template identity.","graph_id":"ecoli-tusa-desulfurase-assay","limitations":"The readout is sulfide release in a reducing biochemical assay. It does not resolve allosteric activation versus sulfur-acceptor turnover, a specific residue's chemistry, intracellular sulfur partitioning or tRNA/Moco synthesis. TusA alone has no detected assay activity. Mixed IscS2/IscU/TusA complexes occur in the study, so mutually exclusive occupancy of an entire IscS dimer is not assumed.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P0A890"],"label":"Purified TusA present with IscS in the cysteine/DTT assay","node_id":"tusa-present-with-iscs","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"IscS sulfide-production activity measured by methylene blue","node_id":"iscs-sulfide-production","node_type":"ACTIVITY"}],"scope":"Recombinant E. coli TusA and IscS in the 2024 purified-protein assay; not all PF01206 members, an isolated domain or intracellular sulfur flux.","scope_status":"MECHANISTIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:562","title":"TusA increases purified IscS sulfide-production activity"},{"context":"Figure 5A/D compares 0, 1, 5, 10 and 50 uM TusA with 50 uM IscU, 25 uM Fe2+, 1 uM IscS and 250 uM L-cysteine in anaerobic 50 mM Tris-HCl, 100 mM NaCl, pH 8. Reductants are either 2 mM DTT or the conjunction of 1 uM Fdx, 1 uM Fpr and 100 uM NADPH. Following 30 min preincubation, IscS and cysteine initiate the reaction. A456 is recorded every 5 min for 40 min in independent triplicates; assay temperature is not specified in the inspected caption.","edges":[{"directness":"UNRESOLVED","edge_id":"equimolar-tusa-decreases-assembly-signal","evidence":[{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01206/olivieri-2024-tusa.txt","cache_sha256":"b124297078a284b15112757262281fe7e0edd4cdbc2a60fdd2f07dd1dc14e4ba","explanation":"Visually inspected Figure 5A/D provides the downward direction at 50 uM; the Results and caption establish the dose dependence, reducing systems and matched no-TusA comparison. The source's assembly interpretation is scoped to the optical readout.","reference":"PMID:38980029","snippet":"it did significantly impact Fe-S cluster assembly","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11302665/"},{"cache_path":"evidence/PF01206/TusA-identity.txt","cache_sha256":"4e512da52d9b77d458bcf81b447c01eee49eb768089e8010c7d2a75c68abcc32","explanation":"Keeps the E. coli reference identity explicit without treating family membership as evidence for the concentration-dependent effect.","reference":"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0A890.json","snippet":"UniProtKB:P0A890; TUSA_ECOLI; tusA, sirA, yhhP; b3470, JW3435.","source_url":"https://rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P0A890.json"}],"evidence_kind":"EXPERIMENTAL","mechanism":"At 50 uM TusA, equimolar with IscU, the A456 time course is lower than the no-TusA control with either reductant system. The observed reduction is retained without converting it into a directly demonstrated sulfur-transfer or binding-competition step.","object":"assembly-associated-a456","predicate":"decreases","subject":"tusa-50um-assembly-condition","support":"OBSERVED"}],"family_mapping":"TusA is mapped to the 81-aa E. coli K12 reference P0A890, PF01206 residues 10-79, not to all TusA-like paralogs. Full experimental clone sequence and template strain remain unverified. IscU was His6-tagged then thrombin-cleaved according to the 2024 Methods.","graph_id":"ecoli-tusa-fes-assembly-readout","limitations":"A456 is a biochemical assembly readout, not direct atom tracing or identification of a inhibited elementary reaction. Lower TusA doses do not show the same clear reduction. Protein competition and sulfur diversion are explanatory models, not additional observed edges. The B/E spectral caption's yellow-line reference is inconsistent with the no-TusA red-line key; only the A/D concentration time courses are adopted.","nodes":[{"grounding":["UniProtKB:P0A890"],"label":"50 uM TusA added to the complete IscS/IscU assembly reaction","node_id":"tusa-50um-assembly-condition","node_type":"PERTURBATION"},{"label":"Fe-S assembly-associated absorbance at 456 nm over time","node_id":"assembly-associated-a456","node_type":"PHENOTYPE"}],"scope":"Concentration-dependent effect of E. coli TusA in the reconstituted IscS/IscU system, retaining the observed optical outcome separately from the proposed sulfur-diversion mechanism.","scope_status":"PHENOTYPIC","taxon":"NCBITaxon:562","title":"Equimolar TusA reduces the IscU Fe-S assembly-associated optical signal"}],"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":12368,"domain_architectures":48,"matches":18447,"proteins":18434,"proteomes":11553,"structures":9,"taxa":16830},"curation_events":[{"action":"CREATE","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065330Z-codex-51fd09.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"changed","summary":"Curate two scoped E. coli TusA causal assay graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:53:30Z"},{"action":"REVIEW","curator":"Codex","event_index":0,"history_record":"history/records/PF01206/2026-10-11T065734Z-codex-7bfcbc.yaml","llm_assisted":true,"outcome":"needs_followup","summary":"Retain partial scientific self-review of TusA assay graphs","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:57:34Z"}],"curation_history":"history/records/PF01206","curation_status":"IN_PROGRESS","description":"This family includes the TusA sulfurtransferases [[cite:PUB00043028]].","discussions":[{"discussion_id":"tusa-sulfur-relay-and-clone-coverage","evidence":[{"evidence_source":"full_text","explanation":"Figures 1 and 5 were visually inspected. Native MS supports mixed complexes, while intracellular concentrations and sulfur partitioning remain proposed explanations.","reference":"PMID:38980029","supports":"PARTIAL"},{"evidence_source":"selected_full_text","explanation":"The cited 2013 Table 1 establishes the pJD34 expression-vector lead, not the complete 2024 clone sequence. Its cellular phenotypes were not independently adopted in this graph batch.","reference":"PMID:23281480","supports":"PARTIAL"}],"kind":"CURATION_TODO","notes":"The 2006 sulfur-relay study PMID:16387657 and additional 2024 TusA/Fur and CyaY studies remain research leads, not inspected edge evidence here. Status remains IN_PROGRESS.","posed_by":"Codex","posed_date":"2026-10-11","prompt":"Resolve the experimental clone sequence and extend primary-evidence coverage to TusA sulfur relay, tRNA thiolation and Moco contexts.","rationale":"Two 2024 assay contexts do not cover the full TusA mechanism or its par